FEX: find a shebang interpreter outside the rootfs too (SteamARM)

GetShebangInterpFile() only looked for the interpreter under FEX's rootfs.
Inside a pressure-vessel container that is not the container's /usr, so
Proton's "#!/usr/bin/env python3" was not recognised as a script; execve
returned ENOEXEC and glibc's execvp ran the Python launcher with /bin/sh
("from: not found", MEASURED). The interpreter is now also looked up as
named.

--- a/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp	2026-09-27 02:13:54
+++ b/Source/Tools/LinuxEmulation/LinuxSyscalls/Syscalls.cpp	2026-09-27 02:13:54
@@ -162,12 +162,20 @@
 
     // If the filename is absolute then prepend the rootfs
     // If it is relative then don't append the rootfs
+    const fextl::string AsNamed = ShebangProgram;
     if (ShebangProgram[0] == '/') {
       ShebangProgram = FEX::HLE::_SyscallHandler->RootFSPath() + ShebangProgram;
     }
 
     if (FHU::Filesystem::Exists(ShebangProgram)) {
       return ShebangProgram;
+    }
+    // Not in the rootfs: the interpreter as the process sees it. Inside a
+    // pressure-vessel container the rootfs is not the container's /usr, and
+    // "#!/usr/bin/env python3" (Proton's own launcher) came back ENOEXEC;
+    // glibc's execvp then ran the Python script with /bin/sh.
+    if (AsNamed[0] == '/' && FHU::Filesystem::Exists(AsNamed)) {
+      return AsNamed;
     }
   }
 
